              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lori Evans"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Lovely! I'm becoming a big fan of trout.\n\nSEANZILLA: 'Amandine' is right, it means \"garnished with almonds.\" Almondine isn't a word in the dictionary."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mojofly05"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Following another recipe, I made sure that the pan was very hot, as hot as it could be without burning the butter. Put the trout in flesh side down, and within just a few minutes that was a beautiful golden brown. Flipped it to the skin side for just 30 seconds, and it was done. \nAlso, added some chopped parsley in with the butter and almonds, and some white pepper and just a squeeze of lemon. \nTrout Amandine is a delicious meal , and this recipe works very well. Loved it.",
            "datePublished": "2018-05-13T13:56:17.040Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ModestFish3847"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have used this Trout Almondine recipe for about a year. I've followed other recipes in the past because our family members are avid lovers of trout fishing in the Sierra Nevadas. So, I've made trout most of my life. This recipe is by far my favorite. I make only one alteration. And that's to roast the almonds in the oven before adding them to the pan to finish with butter. I find them to be more crispy with extra flavor. This is just my preference. I hope you enjoy it as much as my husband and I! 😋",
            "datePublished": "2023-10-06T01:58:24.510Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kac2research"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good and simple. Was so easy to prepare and trout was so fresh, meaty, and nice. We will make again, but I will probably season the trout a bit in some cajun spice or lemon pepper before the flour dusting.",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-03T18:36:22.443Z"
          },
