            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "fendformyself"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My best tasting trout so far. I used my own blend of spices, 2T butter, 1/4 flour to cook one large trout. Instead of cooking the entire fish. I skinned it and took off the head and tail, otherwise the fish was intact. I cooked as directed. No garnish or sauce. Tasty. This reduced prep and cook time by half. Thanks for the idea. I think the flour and butter make the big difference- good texture.",
            "datePublished": "2010-02-27T15:11:18.830Z"
